WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.122 --> 00:00:01.330
SPEAKER: What's up, everyone?

00:00:01.330 --> 00:00:02.705
Thanks for checking
out this week

00:00:02.705 --> 00:00:05.182
in Cloud, where we serve
you the lowest latency news.

00:00:05.182 --> 00:00:07.140
Ever wish you could get
a little more oomph out

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.550
of your virtual machines?

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:11.340
Google's happy to now offer
an expanded range of compute

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:13.047
and memory optimized machines.

00:00:13.047 --> 00:00:14.880
These let you optimize
your virtual machines

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:17.490
for workloads that might
need that extra power.

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:21.060
You can get signed up for early
access now, so get moving.

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:24.270
This week, we're excited to
announce Elastifile for GCP.

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:26.580
With Elastifile, we've
reinvented file storage

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:28.140
as a fully managed service.

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:29.640
This means you get
to take advantage

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:31.920
of all the benefits of a
traditional file storage

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:35.070
system, such as high
availability and easy sharing,

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:36.750
without the hassle
of forecasting,

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:38.850
managing, and provisioning
enterprise storage

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:40.140
all by yourself.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:42.540
Features like petabyte
capacity and auto scaling

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:45.060
make high-performance
compute jobs easier than ever

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:46.980
while built-in controls
allow you to optimize

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.770
for price or performance.

00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:50.520
Find out how you can
improve your workflow

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:53.460
with Elastifile for GCP.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:55.290
Last year, we announced
Cloud Memorystore

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:58.440
for Redis, our fully managed
in-memory datastore service.

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:01.230
And because users responded
by adopting so quickly,

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:03.510
this year, we're excited to
announce Cloud Memorystore

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:07.350
support for Redis version
4.0, available in beta as well

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:09.870
as a new manual failover API.

00:01:09.870 --> 00:01:11.400
Learn how to access
the new version

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:14.010
and tour smart new features
like cached improvement

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:16.470
and active memory
defragmentation.

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:19.000
You're already running
infrastructure as code, right?

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:20.250
No?

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:22.320
What if you need to
quickly replicate VMs

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:24.390
between environments,
or track changes,

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:28.020
or scale your configuration by
the thousands for production?

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:29.730
The good news is
that with GCP, you

00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:32.790
can use Deployment Manager
or the ever-popular Terraform

00:01:32.790 --> 00:01:34.217
without any additional setup.

00:01:34.217 --> 00:01:36.300
You'll be able to make
changes to your environment

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:39.270
in a way that can be tested,
audited, and automatically

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:42.130
applied, according to your
change management processes,

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:44.160
allowing your app to
scale effortlessly

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:46.165
with massive
increases in demand.

00:01:46.165 --> 00:01:47.790
Read everything you
need to know to get

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:52.020
started running infrastructure
as code today on the GCP blog.

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:53.190
The secret's out.

00:01:53.190 --> 00:01:55.380
We're making our BigQuery
migration bundle offer

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:57.450
generally available to everyone.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:59.100
That means in
addition to BigQuery,

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:01.170
you'll get proof of
concept funding support,

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:03.210
expert advice on
architecture design,

00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:05.760
and online courses
at no extra cost.

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:08.130
Find out why an independent
analysis firm concluded

00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:09.900
that enterprise
customers could save up

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:13.770
to 52% on total cost of
ownership over three years

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:15.107
by switching to the Cloud.

00:02:15.107 --> 00:02:17.190
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:19.380
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:20.550
Have thoughts or ideas?

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:22.000
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

